IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`

§ `Chapter 5A -- Criminal conspiracy`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 120A, 120B.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 120A(1) -- Definition`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 120A(1)"
@export Decide whether the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy under Penal Code 1871 section 120A(1)
GIVEN c IS A Conspiracy @desc An agreement between two distinct persons to commit an offence or cause an offence to be committed. ss 120A(2) and (3) are preservative: unknown impossibility and the other person lack of intent do not defeat party status.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy` IF
        c's `there is an agreement to commit or cause an offence`
    AND NOT (c's `the person` EQUALS c's `the other person`)

§§ `Section 120A(4) and (5) -- Extraterritorial reach`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 120A(4) and (5)"
@export Decide whether Singapore has jurisdiction over the conspiracy under Penal Code 1871 sections 120A(4) and 120A(5)
GIVEN c IS A Conspiracy @desc location of the subject offence is wholly in Singapore or wholly outside Singapore. For an offence outside Singapore, some conspiracy acts must have been done in Singapore and the subject offence must be one that would be an offence if committed in Singapore.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore has jurisdiction over the conspiracy` IF
    CONSIDER c's `location of the subject offence`
    WHEN `wholly in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `partly in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `wholly outside Singapore` THEN
            c's `any acts of the conspiracy were done in Singapore`
        AND c's `the subject offence would be an offence if committed in Singapore`

§§ `Combined`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 120A and 120B"
@export Decide whether the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy within the reach of Singapore law
GIVEN c IS A Conspiracy @desc Conjunction of the s 120A(1) party-status test and the s 120A(4)/(5) jurisdiction test.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy within the reach of Singapore law` IF
        `the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy` c
    AND `Singapore has jurisdiction over the conspiracy` c

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a criminal conspiracy` IF
        `the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy within the reach of Singapore law` (a's `conspiracy`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

§§ `Illustrations`

`Alice and Bob fraud in Singapore` MEANS Conspiracy WITH
    `the person` IS "Alice"
    `the other person` IS "Bob"
    `there is an agreement to commit or cause an offence` IS TRUE
    `the subject offence would be an offence if committed in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `location of the subject offence` IS `wholly in Singapore`
    `the other person intends to carry out the agreement` IS TRUE
    `facts unknown to the person make commission impossible` IS FALSE
    `any acts of the conspiracy were done in Singapore` IS TRUE

`Alice with herself` MEANS Conspiracy WITH
    `the person` IS "Alice"
    `the other person` IS "Alice"
    `there is an agreement to commit or cause an offence` IS TRUE
    `the subject offence would be an offence if committed in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `location of the subject offence` IS `wholly in Singapore`
    `the other person intends to carry out the agreement` IS TRUE
    `facts unknown to the person make commission impossible` IS FALSE
    `any acts of the conspiracy were done in Singapore` IS TRUE

`theft in London planned in London` MEANS Conspiracy WITH
    `the person` IS "Alice"
    `the other person` IS "Bob"
    `there is an agreement to commit or cause an offence` IS TRUE
    `the subject offence would be an offence if committed in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `location of the subject offence` IS `wholly outside Singapore`
    `the other person intends to carry out the agreement` IS TRUE
    `facts unknown to the person make commission impossible` IS FALSE
    `any acts of the conspiracy were done in Singapore` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy` `Alice and Bob fraud in Singapore`
#ASSERT `the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy within the reach of Singapore law` `Alice and Bob fraud in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a party to a criminal conspiracy` `Alice with herself`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Singapore has jurisdiction over the conspiracy` `theft in London planned in London`)

